==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|pero|lang=ru}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|(s)per-|lang=ru}}. Cognates include Ancient Greek [[πτερόν]] (“wing”; “feather”), Lithuanian ''spar̃nas'', and Old Armenian {{term|թիռ||tr=tʿiṙ|flight|lang=xcl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-перо.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|[pʲɪˈro]|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
'''перо''' (peró) ''n'', перья (pér’ja) ''pl''

# [[feather]]
# [[plume]]
# [[pen]]
# {{context|criminal|_|slang|lang=ru}} [[knife]]

